.idea
/node_modules
**/node_modules 
/build
**/build
/dist
*/dist
**/dist
**/dist-cjs
/coverage
**/coverage
*.iml
.aws-sam/*
*.zip
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
.rollup.cache
**/.rollup.cache
*.d.ts.map
*.d.ts
# ...but hand-written declarations belong in source control. The blanket *.d.ts
# rule above exists for emitted output (dist-types/, dist/), and it silently
# swallowed a new ambient declaration -- which also means Biome never sees such a
# file, since vcs.useIgnoreFile is on. Anything authored under a src/ tree is a
# source file and is tracked.
!**/src/**/*.d.ts
*.tgz

# Nothing passes --cache today, but ESLint still runs here (the plugin package's
# own rules, and the examples package that exercises them), so keep ignoring its
# cache. Dropping this line un-ignored a stray cache file and got it committed.
.eslintcache

# VS Code
# settings.json and extensions.json are tracked deliberately (force-added): they
# pin the formatter identity and recommend the extensions that provide it.
.vscode/

# Environment files
.secrets
.env
.env.local

# Node version
.nvmrc
mise.toml

*.rollup.cache

# Durable executions local emulator files
**/.durable-executions-local/
# Scratch space for the LLRT container test (bundles, Dockerfile, image context).
.github/workflows/scripts/llrt/.cloud-work/
